        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edgewater%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community grew around London Town, a 100‑acre tobacco port founded in 1683 that once served as Anne Arundel County’s first seat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Edgewater,_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic London Town and Gardens spans 23 acres, preserving colonial buildings including the National Historic Landmark William Brown House.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Edgewater,_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Edgewater Park offers baseball fields, playgrounds, and riverfront trails managed by Anne Arundel County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
